// flashcard drill — JAH HVAC Trade Database — What HVAC techs do (jahdb demo program)
var ITEMS=[["What HVAC techs do","HVAC technicians install and service heating, ventilation, and air conditioning: furnaces, heat pumps, AC condensers, ductwork, and controls. It blends mechanical, electrical, and refrigeration skills, and EPA certificat"], ["Essential tools","Manifold gauge set, vacuum pump, refrigerant scale, leak detector, multimeter, clamp meter, thermometers, tubing cutter and flaring tools, nitrogen regulator, and a good drill set. Pros add: combustion analyzer, duct bla"], ["Key skills","Refrigeration cycle diagnostics (superheat/subcooling), electrical troubleshooting, brazing copper line sets, airflow measurement and duct design, combustion analysis on furnaces, and reading wiring diagrams. Diagnostics"], ["Safety essentials","Refrigerant displaces oxygen and can cause frostbite \u2014 ventilate and wear gloves. High voltage and capacitors: discharge before touching. Brazing needs fire watch. Ladders and attics: heat exhaustion is the silent killer"], ["Getting started","Trade school or apprenticeship, then EPA Section 608 certification (legally required). NATE certification boosts pay. Start in residential install or maintenance, specialize later in commercial or controls."], ["Pro tips","Check the simple things first: filters, breakers, thermostats, disconnects. Document superheat/subcooling on every call. Keep condensers clean \u2014 most no-cooling calls are airflow. Sell maintenance agreements; they are re"], ["Refrigerant","Trade term \u2014 Refrigerant: The working fluid carrying heat; modern types include R-410A and R-32."], ["Superheat","Trade term \u2014 Superheat: Refrigerant temperature above boiling at the evaporator; key diagnostic."], ["Subcooling","Trade term \u2014 Subcooling: Refrigerant temperature below condensing at the condenser; key diagnostic."], ["Compressor","Trade term \u2014 Compressor: The pump pressurizing refrigerant; the heart of the system."], ["Condenser","Trade term \u2014 Condenser: The outdoor coil rejecting heat."], ["Evaporator","Trade term \u2014 Evaporator: The indoor coil absorbing heat."], ["TXV","Trade term \u2014 TXV: Thermostatic expansion valve metering refrigerant into the evaporator."], ["Heat pump","Trade term \u2014 Heat pump: A reversible AC that heats by moving heat indoors."], ["SEER","Trade term \u2014 SEER: Seasonal energy efficiency ratio for cooling."], ["AFUE","Trade term \u2014 AFUE: Annual fuel utilization efficiency for furnaces."], ["HSPF","Trade term \u2014 HSPF: Heating seasonal performance factor for heat pumps."], ["MERV","Trade term \u2014 MERV: Filter efficiency rating; higher traps smaller particles."], ["CFM","Trade term \u2014 CFM: Cubic feet per minute of airflow."], ["Static pressure","Trade term \u2014 Static pressure: Resistance to airflow in ducts."], ["Brazing","Trade term \u2014 Brazing: High-temperature copper joining with filler rod."], ["Nitrogen purge","Trade term \u2014 Nitrogen purge: Flowing nitrogen while brazing to prevent internal oxidation."], ["Recovery","Trade term \u2014 Recovery: Legally required capture of refrigerant before opening systems."], ["Combustion analysis","Trade term \u2014 Combustion analysis: Measuring furnace exhaust for safe, efficient burning."], ["Zoning","Trade term \u2014 Zoning: Dampers and controls for different areas."]];
